exports[`schema_to_skill_docs generateObjectiveDoc matches snapshot 1`] = `
"# Objectives and Error Budgets

## Budgeting Methods

- \`occurrences\`: Occurrences: SLI = good events / total events over the time window. Use for request-based SLOs.
- \`timeslices\`: Timeslices: the time window is cut into slices of timesliceWindow; a slice is good when its ratio ≥ timesliceTarget. SLI = good slices / total slices. Use for time-based SLOs. Requires timesliceTarget and timesliceWindow in objective, and sli.metric.timeslice indicator if using metric comparisons.

## Time Windows

- **rolling**: sliding window, continuously updated. Allowed durations: \`7d\`, \`30d\`, \`90d\`.
- **calendarAligned**: resets at the start of each calendar period. Allowed durations: \`1w\`, \`1M\`.

## Error Budget Math

error budget = 1 − \`target\`

consumed budget = bad fraction ÷ error budget

Example: target \`0.999\` over a \`30d\` rolling window ⇒ 0.1% error budget ≈ 43.2 minutes of bad events.

## Constraints

- \`target\` must be strictly between 0 and 1 (exclusive). Example: \`0.999\` = 99.9%.
- \`timesliceTarget\` and \`timesliceWindow\` are **required** when \`budgetingMethod\` is \`\\"timeslices\\"\`. They are ignored for \`\\"occurrences\\"\`.
- \`timesliceWindow\` accepts \`m\` or \`h\` units (e.g. \`\\"5m\\"\`, \`\\"1h\\"\`) and must be shorter than the time window.
- \`sli.metric.timeslice\` indicator requires \`budgetingMethod: \\"timeslices\\"\`."
`;

exports[`schema_to_skill_docs generateSloIndicatorsDoc matches snapshot 1`] = `
"# SLO Indicator Types

\`indicator\` defines how the SLI is computed. Pick the variant by data source.
Each indicator type maps to a specific \`type\` discriminator value.

#### \`type: \\"sli.apm.transactionDuration\\"\`

Use for APM latency SLIs. Measures the ratio of APM transactions faster than a given latency threshold.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.apm.transactionDuration\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |

#### \`type: \\"sli.apm.transactionErrorRate\\"\`

Use for APM error-rate SLIs. Measures the ratio of APM transactions that did not result in an error.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.apm.transactionErrorRate\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |

#### \`type: \\"sli.synthetics.availability\\"\`

Use for Synthetics monitor availability SLIs. Measures the ratio of successful monitor checks.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.synthetics.availability\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |

#### \`type: \\"sli.kql.custom\\"\`

Use for custom KQL-based SLIs on any index. Define good and total event populations with KQL filters.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.kql.custom\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |

#### \`type: \\"sli.metric.custom\\"\`

Use for custom metric-aggregation SLIs. Define good and total as math equations over field aggregations.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.metric.custom\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |

#### \`type: \\"sli.metric.timeslice\\"\`

Use for timeslice-based metric SLIs. Only valid with budgetingMethod: \\"timeslices\\". The time window is divided into slices; a slice is good when the metric equation satisfies the comparator threshold.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.metric.timeslice\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |

#### \`type: \\"sli.histogram.custom\\"\`

Use for histogram-based SLIs. Define good and total event populations using value_count or range aggregations on a pre-aggregated histogram field.

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| \`type\` | \\"sli.histogram.custom\\" | required |  |
| \`params\` | object | required |  |"
`;
